  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** MediaAlpha’s core auto insurance advertising platform is riding strong carrier demand, with record first‑quarter sales driven by a favorable mix shift to its open marketplace and broader insurer participation. The under‑65 health insurance vertical, however, remains a drag, clouding otherwise robust momentum and muting profitability. The digital insurance‑advertising environment appears supportive, as carriers lean into transparent, scalable acquisition channels.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** The team beat revenue guidance but missed consensus earnings, a gap tied to the health‑segment drag and investment spending. Even so, management is returning capital aggressively, planning to exhaust a large share‑repurchase program this year—a signal of conviction in the auto‑marketplace franchise. Execution priorities center on AI‑powered targeting and deeper carrier relationships; the EPS miss tempers but does not derail an otherwise confident operational narrative.",
